# Suppresses /etc/xdg/autostart/im-launch.desktop, from Debian's im-config.
#
# home/apps.nix links this ONE FILE, by build-time-resolved store path, into
# ~/.config/autostart/ via xdg.configFile. The name must match the entry it
# suppresses exactly -- XDG matches autostart entries by file name, and
# ~/.config/autostart wins over /etc/xdg/autostart. See
# ./org.kde.xwaylandvideobridge.desktop for why the directory is not linked
# whole.
#
# This switches ibus off. There is no input method on this machine, by choice.
#
# What it did. im-launch starts an input method the X11 way: it reads
# /usr/share/im-config/xinputrc.common, picks an input method, and runs it. With
# no ~/.xinputrc here, /etc/X11/xinit/xinputrc says `run_im default`, which
# auto-selected ibus -- nothing on this machine chose it. The result was
# `ibus-daemon --daemonize --xim`: ibus as an X11 input method, in a Wayland
# session.
#
# Why it showed up. uwsm runs XDG autostart; the session this repo carried
# before it did not. So this entry first ran under Hyprland on 2026-08-07
# 21:15:19, the first uwsm login. The starts before that are Plasma sessions.
#
# What went wrong. ibus-ui-gtk3 checks its own footing on Wayland, and posts a
# desktop notification titled "IBus Notification" when it finds ibus started as
# an X11 input method while GTK_IM_MODULE and QT_IM_MODULE point at it. That
# notification is the reason this file exists. ibus offers no setting to
# silence it -- checked every key in all three org.freedesktop.ibus schemas.
#
# The first attempt at this kept ibus and took the notification's advice: a
# sibling entry started ibus as a proper Wayland input method, and ../uwsm/env
# unset the two variables. That worked -- Hyprland handed ibus a real
# zwp_input_method_v2 and activated it against a focused field, traced under
# WAYLAND_DEBUG. It was removed anyway, on 2026-08-08, because ibus-ui-gtk3
# segfaults on this machine:
#
#   2026-07-15 16:22, 17:21, 18:29 | X11 ibus, under Plasma
#   2026-07-16 07:21               | X11 ibus, under Plasma
#   2026-08-08 18:50, 19:15        | the Wayland panel
#
# Six SIGSEGVs in three weeks, in both modes, four of them predating any of this
# work. The crash is a Debian/ibus bug, not a configuration fault, and no config
# here can fix it. What the Wayland panel changed was visibility: under
# im-launch the unit's ExecStart exited 0 immediately and a crashing panel
# failed nothing, whereas the panel WAS its unit's MainPID, so every segfault
# became a failed unit and a fumon notification.
#
# So it goes. ibus carried one engine here, xkb:us::eng -- a plain US layout
# identical to hyprland.lua's kb_layout -- so it provided nothing that XKB does
# not, and nothing on this machine ever chose it. ../uwsm/env still unsets
# GTK_IM_MODULE and QT_IM_MODULE, which matters more now than it did: with no
# ibus running, those variables would point GTK and Qt at a client library for
# a daemon that is not there.
#
# To get an input method back, run `ibus-setup`, add a real engine, and restore
# the deleted entry from git history -- or install fcitx5, which speaks
# zwp_input_method_v2 natively and does not have this crash.
#
# To undo: remove the xdg.configFile."autostart/im-launch.desktop" entry from
# home/apps.nix and switch again -- deleting the symlink by hand does not
# stick, the next switch's linkGeneration recreates it. Then
# `systemctl --user daemon-reload` and log back in.
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=im-launch
Hidden=true
